A second SALT/RSS spectrum was taken at 16:58:32 UTC on 2017 August 19 with the same setting as the first, with an exposure time of 716 s. The trace of the transient was still clearly visible in the twilight though the resulting spectrum is of low signal-to-noise ratio (S/N). A third spectrum was taken on the following night but it was too contaminated by background to be useful.

